    "answer": {
      "short": "Amplitudes $1$; periods $2\\pi,\\pi,\\frac{2\\pi}3,\\frac\\pi2$, giving $1,2,3,4$ complete cycles.",
      "worked": "For $y=\\sin nx$, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi}{n}$. Plot quarter-cycle points at $x=\\frac{k\\pi}{2n}$ with ordinates repeating $0,1,0,-1$. For $n=1,2,3,4$, continue to $2\\pi$ and join smoothly on the same axes. All four curves pass through $(0,0)$, $(\\pi,0)$ and $(2\\pi,0)$.",
